<sect1 id="chapter11_1autotoc_md43_1s1"><sect2 id="chapter11_1autotoc_md43">
<title>Error reporting</title><para>Surface Lua errors to callers and logs explicitly. Do not swallow script failures inside binding wrappers. Keep ownership clear: runtime owns <computeroutput>lua_State</computeroutput> lifecycle.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".text"><codeline><highlight class="normal">//<sp/>Lua<sp/>errors<sp/>should<sp/>propagate<sp/>to<sp/>the<sp/>caller<sp/>in<sp/>a<sp/>clear<sp/>way.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">//<sp/>The<sp/>binding<sp/>layer<sp/>should<sp/>not<sp/>hide<sp/>the<sp/>failure<sp/>origin.</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
